    "description": "<p><span style=\"color:rgb(239, 230, 216);font-family:Montserrat, sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;orphans:2;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;widows:2;word-spacing:0px;-webkit-text-stroke-width:0px;white-space:normal;background-color:rgba(24, 22, 46, 0.753);text-decoration-thickness:initial;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;display:inline !important;float:none\">Passive: You sense the surface emotions of creatures within Close range on scene. This does not reveal specific thoughts or secrets, only general states.</span></p><p></p><p>Action: You can mark 1 stress to enhance one emotion among a group of people or to weaken it, you can not create emotion for people if their don`t feel this at moment like love, fear.</p><p></p><p>Action Per Rest: Once per scene  you can spent 1 fear to raise the morale of allies at far distances, they will clean 1d4 stress after that.</p>",
